# Pace — environment variables that are NOT Worker secrets (those go into
# apps/api/.dev.vars locally, see apps/api/.dev.vars.example).
#
# Each tool reads its own file: Vite reads apps/web/.env*, the Expo CLI reads
# apps/app/.env*, Playwright and the LLM scripts read the shell environment.
# `cp .env.example apps/web/.env` is enough for local web development; export the
# others in your shell when you need them. All values below are the local defaults.

# ── Web (Vite, apps/web/.env) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# API origin the browser talks to (no proxy: CORS + bearer). Production: https://pace-api.nalinor.dev
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Username of the Telegram bot shown by the Login Widget (no @).
VITE_TELEGRAM_BOT=PaceTaskTrackerBot

# ── Android app (Expo CLI, apps/app/.env) ──────────────────────────────────────
# API origin baked into the app (app.config.ts → extra.apiUrl). Defaults to production.
# Use your machine's LAN address for a device on the same network.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8787

# ── Playwright (shell) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run the e2e suite against an already running stack instead of starting wrangler dev + vite preview.
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4173
# Use an installed Chromium instead of `bunx playwright install` (sandboxes, CI images).
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=/usr/bin/chromium

# ── LLM regression, stage 2 (shell; `bun test:llm`) ────────────────────────────
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
